    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look toward a pivotal slate today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 efficiency score makes him the clear centerpiece of the offense. Benefiting from a favorable 16% park factor adjustment and a prime spot in the #2 hole against Flaherty, **Gunnar Henderson** is poised to capitalize on his elite platoon profile. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.35) and **Josh Jung** (63.99) also grade out as strong starts; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is maximized by a 14% platoon boost against Elder, while **Josh Jung** stands to gain significant value from a soft matchup against Rodriguez, whose 5.91 xERA represents the most exploitable pitching vulnerability in our current rotation.\n\nOur bench logic was refined by tight margins, with **Nolan Schanuel** (41.65) narrowly missing the cut behind the more efficient profile of **Coby Mayo** (48.97). While **Nolan Schanuel** receives a solid bump for his projected #3 spot in the order, the combination of a high-difficulty matchup against deGrom and the aggregate efficiency of the utility slot pushed him to the pine. We are monitoring **Sam Antonacci** (48.07) closely, as he occupies a high-upside spot against McDonald; the wind blowing out adds a critical variable that could push his production above the current projection. We remain cautious regarding **Kyle Tucker** (53.10) and **Andy Pages** (44.57), both of whom are facing the hurdle of a tough 3.08 xERA assignment against Henderson. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill** currently unavailable, we are emphasizing daily efficiency over raw volume to preserve our cap space for late-week pivots.",
